## Rows skipped (with reason)

- a20 P2 / b10 P2 — space thousands separators ("500 000", "1 579 589"). SKIPPED: ACCEPTED-ROUND lists "requests for space thousands separators" as a standing skip, and the checker confirms it: `NUMBER_THOUSAND_STYLE.fi = 'dot'` in scripts/check-column-translation.mjs, so a space-grouped figure is parsed as two numbers and `numbers` FAILs. Dot grouping kept in all 18 files (incl. the reformatted 006 fines in a15).
- a22 P2 / b11 P2 — remove U+200B, and turn 003 Q16–Q20 into `##` headings. SKIPPED, two independent reasons:
  1. `checkBlocks` compares `countZwsp(source.body)` with the target and FAILs on any difference. The Korean canonical source carries the identical counts (003: 52 in src/content/columns/ and 52 in columns-fi; 005: 8 and 8; 013: 5 and 5), and the sibling locales sv/da/nb/de carry the same 52 in 003 — the blanks are a source artifact, not a Finnish defect. Same for the `**​**` empty bold lines in 005: 4 in the Korean source, 4 in fi, 4 in sv, 0 only in the EN rewrite.
  2. Making Q16–Q20 headings would break `checkHeadings`: the English source itself has them as plain body lines (columns-en/003 line 199 "Q16. After an accident, …"), and ACCEPTED-ROUND forbids adding new headings.
- a21 P2 — PARTIAL, not fully applied. Every remaining bare "1"/"2"/"3" was tested individually against the checker (script kept at .tmp-fi/trydigit.py); each of the following made `numbers` FAIL with "missing from translation", because the Korean source carries the same digit and the checker's Finnish word-numeral lexicon (`buildFiLexicon`) only recognises the nominative phrases "yksi vuosi/vuotta/kuukausi/kuukautta/päivä(ä)/viikko(a)/henkilö(ä)" and bare "kaksi…kymmenen" — every inflected Finnish form ("yhden", "kahden", "kolmena") is invisible to it. Kept in digit form per RULEBOOK R6 / ACCEPTED-ROUND ("keep the previous form for that number and note it"): 001 "alle 1 vuoden" (x4), "olemassa 1 vuoden tai pidempään" (x4); 002 "kuitataan 1 tilillä", "päätettyinä 1 ilmoituksella"; 004 "tavallisesti 2 kuukauden verokaudelta"; 005 "enemmän kuin 1 ulkomaan kansalaisen"; 008 "täyttä 1 palvelusvuotta" (x2), "kutakin 1 vuotta kohden" (x2), "3 peräkkäisenä päivänä" (x3). All of these are grammatically well formed when the digit is read in the required case ("alle yhden vuoden", "kolmena peräkkäisenä päivänä"); what remains is the style preference the reviewer raises.

