## Where I think the reviewer was wrong (not applied)

1. fi-a row 21, quote "alle 1 vuotta" — that string does not exist in columns-fi/001; the file reads "alle 1 vuoden", which is grammatical (alle + genitive). The row's other listed instances do exist and were handled as described above.
2. fi-a row 20 / fi-b row 10 — Finnish does group thousands with a space, so the reviewer is right about Finnish usage, but the campaign's checker for fi is pinned to dot grouping and ACCEPTED-ROUND makes this a standing skip. Flagged here as a real residual defect that only a checker change can fix.
3. fi-a row 22 / fi-b row 11 — removing the U+200B blanks and promoting Q16–Q20 to headings would improve the Finnish reading, but the blanks and the plain-line Q16–Q20 come from the shared canonical source (identical in ko, sv, da, nb, de) and both the ZWSP count and the heading levels are pinned to it by the checker. This is a source-level layout decision, not a Finnish-locale one.
4. fi-a row 7 — the reviewer asks to restore "courts generally impose", which partly reverses RULEBOOK R3's softening of the same sentence. I applied the reviewer's version but kept an explicit guarantee denial ("kyse ei ole taatusta seuraamuksesta") in both the 3-month and the 4/6-month sentences, so R3's advertising-safety purpose is preserved. Worth a supervisor ruling if R3 is meant to override the round-5 row.
5. fi-a row 15 — the suggested rewrite also respaced the amounts ("40 000 TWD"); I kept "TWD 40.000 (新臺幣)" (dot grouping, existing currency order) for the checker, and applied only the attribution fix the row is actually about.

